# PDF and JPEG demonstration materials are byte-exact artefacts. The PDF cross-
# reference table is a fixed-width record format whose rows end in a mandatory
# space, and every entry in it is a byte offset into the file, so any end-of-line
# normalisation shifts the offsets and the document stops opening. The same
# applies to JPEG entropy-coded data. `binary` is `-text -diff -merge`: no
# conversion on checkout, no line-based diff, no line-based merge.
*.pdf binary
*.jpg binary
